def shell(route,title,content,scripts=''):
 links=''.join(f'<a href="/{r}"'+(' aria-current="page"' if r==route else '')+f'>[ {label.upper()} ]</a>' for r,label in nav)
 out=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>BATTERY / {title}</title><meta name="description" content="Reserve policies and recoverable owned agents. Real local AI recovery evidence, live Solana mainnet/devnet, confirmed bounded USDC canary, open source."><meta name="theme-color" content="#000000"><meta property="og:title" content="BATTERY / {title}"><meta property="og:description" content="Cut the fees. Keep the work. Agent reserve and recovery tools."><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:url" content="{BASE}/{route}"><meta property="og:image" content="{BASE}/assets/brand/banner-1500x500.png"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><link rel="canonical" href="{BASE}/{route}"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/brand/favicon-32.png"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/brand/logo-180.png"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"><script type="module" src="/surface.mjs"></script>{scripts}</head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><div class="page"><header class="masthead"><a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="BATTERY home"><pre id="brand-symbol" aria-hidden="true"></pre><pre id="brand-art" aria-hidden="true">BATTERY</pre></a><div class="mast-note">A reserve for agents<br>with work left to do.</div><div class="mast-actions"><span class="edition">SDK v0.3 / MAINNET CANARY VERIFIED</span><a class="text-button" href="/status">[ RELEASE STATUS ]</a></div></header><nav class="product-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">{links}</nav><main id="main">{content}</main><footer><span>BATTERY / SDK v0.3</span><a href="/agents.md">[ AGENTS.MD ]</a><a href="/docs#privacy">[ DATA + LIMITS ]</a></footer></div></body></html>'''
 (D/(route+'.html' if route else 'index.html')).write_text(out)
def head(serial,title,desc):return f'<div class="bench-head"><div><span class="serial">{serial}</span><h1>{title}</h1></div><p>{desc}</p></div>'
def panel(title,body):return f'<section class="panel"><h2>{title}</h2>{body}</section>'
portrait='''<div class="device home-device"><button id="portrait-motion" class="portrait-motion text-button" aria-label="Pause portrait animation" aria-pressed="false" hidden>[ PAUSE ]</button><pre id="agent-face" class="ascii-face" aria-hidden="true"></pre><span class="device-serial">AGENT 01 / WORK LEFT TO DO</span></div>'''
shell('','Keep the work',f'''<section class="home-hero"><div class="home-copy"><span class="serial">AGENT RESERVE / RECOVERY / 001</span><h1>THE FEES STOP.<br>THE WORK DOESN'T<br>HAVE TO.</h1><p>An agent shouldn't spend its last dollar guessing. Give it a protected reserve, a permitted cheaper route, and a place to resume.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-button primary-link" href="/evidence">[ WATCH THE RECOVERY &gt; ]</a><a class="text-button" href="/docs#quickstart">[ RUN THE LOCAL KIT ]</a></div><p class="fine">Real local models. Live Solana mainnet research.<br>Mainnet canary finalized. All USDC returned.<br>Blackout lab uses paper balances.</p></div>{portrait}</section><section class="product-grid">{panel('01 / SET THE BOUNDARY','<p>Name a policy. Protect a balance. Decide whether a cheaper route is allowed before the blackout.</p><a href="/policies" class="text-button">[ YOUR POLICIES &gt; ]</a>')}{panel('02 / PULL THE PLUG','<p>Turn fee income off. Exhaust the provider allowance. Check which constraint stops the next task.</p><a href="/lab" class="text-button">[ BLACKOUT LAB &gt; ]</a>')}{panel('03 / KEEP THE RECEIPT','<p>Record the scenario. Inspect its execution log. Export it and re-run the same policy later.</p><a href="/runs" class="text-button">[ TEST JOURNAL &gt; ]</a>')}</section><section class="panel release-strip"><div><span class="serial">CURRENT RELEASE</span><h2>TRY IT. BREAK IT. INSPECT IT.</h2><p>Qwen to Llama. Mainnet research and actual recovery. Bounded mainnet delegation, real recovery, three settlements. Revoke confirmed; all USDC returned.</p></div><a class="text-button" href="/evidence">[ SHOW THE EVIDENCE &gt; ]</a></section>''','<script type="module" src="/legacy.mjs"></script>')
old=(SITE/'lab-template.html').read_text();body=old.split('<main>')[1].split('</main>')[0];body=body.split('<section id="proof"')[0]
workspace='''<section class="panel lab-save"><div><span class="serial">POLICY WORKSPACE / THIS BROWSER</span><label for="policy-name">Policy name</label><input id="policy-name" class="text-input" maxlength="80" value="My blackout policy" autocomplete="off"></div><div class="actions"><button id="save-policy" type="button" class="text-button">[ SAVE POLICY ]</button><button id="new-policy" type="button" class="text-button">[ SAVE AS NEW ]</button><button id="record-test" type="button" class="text-button">[ RECORD TEST ]</button><a href="/runs" class="text-button">[ JOURNAL ]</a></div><p id="workspace-status" role="status" class="fine">Saved locally on this device. Export from Policies to move your workspace. A recorded test is a simulation, not a paid receipt.</p></section>'''
body=body.replace('<section id="blackout"',workspace+'<section id="blackout"')
dialog=old.split('<dialog id="guide">')[1].split('</dialog>')[0]
# Keep existing guide handlers working, with a contextual builder-notes button.
body+=f'<div class="actions below-lab"><button id="open-guide" class="text-button">[ BUILDER NOTES ]</button><a href="/docs" class="text-button">[ INTEGRATION DOCS ]</a></div><dialog id="guide">{dialog}</dialog>'
body=body.replace('href="battery-pilot-kit.zip"','href="/battery-pilot-kit.zip"')
shell('lab','Blackout lab',body,'<script type="module" src="/lab-workspace.mjs"></script>')
def preset(name,s,desc):
 query=html.escape('#'+__import__('urllib.parse',fromlist=['urlencode']).urlencode({'test':json.dumps(s,separators=(',',':'))}),quote=True)
 return panel(name,f'<p>{desc}</p><a href="/lab{query}" class="text-button">[ USE PRESET &gt; ]</a>')
default=dict(reserve=100,rate=1,floor=10,provider=24,fallback=True,crash=True,fees=False)
shell('policies','Policies',head('01 / LOCAL WORKSPACE','SET THE BOUNDARY.','Your agent. Your limits.<br>Saved in this browser, exportable as JSON.')+'''<section class="panel"><div class="section-top"><h2>YOUR POLICIES</h2><div class="actions"><a class="text-button" href="/lab">[ NEW POLICY ]</a><button id="export-workspace" class="text-button">[ EXPORT ALL ]</button><label class="text-button import-label">[ IMPORT JSON ]<input id="import-workspace" type="file" accept="application/json,.json" aria-label="Import workspace JSON"></label></div></div><p id="workspace-status" class="fine" role="status">Policies and tests stay in this browser, separately for each domain. Export on the old domain, then import here to move them. Keep an export before clearing site data.</p><div id="policy-list"></div></section><span class="serial preset-title">START FROM A PRESET / ILLUSTRATIVE COSTS</span><div class="product-grid">'''+preset('RESERVE FIRST',default,'$100 reserve. $10 protected. Cheaper route approved.')+preset('STRICT PRIMARY',{**default,'fallback':False},'Same reserve. No alternate route. Provider allowance becomes the stop.')+preset('SMALL SURVIVOR',{**default,'reserve':5,'floor':1,'provider':0},'A $5 reserve with $1 protected. Economy route only.')+'</div>','<script type="module" src="/workspace.mjs"></script>')
shell('runs','Test journal',head('02 / RECORDED SCENARIOS','KEEP THE RECEIPT.','Every saved test has its policy.<br>Re-run it, inspect it, take it with you.')+'''<section class="panel"><div class="section-top"><h2>TEST JOURNAL</h2><a href="/lab" class="text-button">[ NEW BLACKOUT ]</a></div><p id="workspace-status" class="fine" role="status">Local simulation history. No real model tasks or funds were used. Results are recomputed with the recorded engine version.</p><div id="run-list"></div></section>''','<script type="module" src="/workspace.mjs"></script>')
shell('status','Release status',head('03 / VERIFIED VS UNVERIFIED','SHOW THE EVIDENCE.','A useful preview is live.<br>A paid agent service is not ready.')+'''<section class="panel"><span class="serial">RELEASE GATE</span><h2>[ DEVELOPER PREVIEW / GO ]</h2><p>Explore policies, run illustrative blackouts, keep a local test journal, and verify the paper ledger on your machine.</p><div class="gate-list"><p>[ PASS ] 20 Python ledger/adapter checks; offline Node boundaries and 15 local program checks.</p><p>[ PASS ] Real Qwen + Llama local inference and forced-exit recovery. <a href="/evidence">Inspect proof.</a></p><p>[ PASS ] Live public Solana devnet RPC integration. <a href="/live">Read a sample.</a></p><p>[ HOLD ] No authenticated provider billing / maximum-cost adapter.</p><p>[ HOLD ] No paid model workload or third-party runtime migration.</p><p>[ HOLD ] Devnet memo tool tested, faucet refused funding; no confirmed checkpoint transaction.</p><p>[ PASS ] Existing mainnet USDC delegation program executed in local LiteSVM: 15 checks. <a href="/mainnet">Inspect scope.</a></p><p>[ PASS ] Bounded mainnet canary: 8 finalized transactions, 3 result settlements, recovery, revoke and all 5 USDC returned. <a href="/mainnet">Inspect receipts.</a> No hosted vault or token.</p><p>[ HOLD ] No uninterrupted 72-hour observer proof.</p></div><a href="/docs#quickstart" class="text-button">[ REPRODUCE THE PAPER CHECKS ]</a></section><section class="panel"><div class="section-top"><h2>READ-ONLY OBSERVER</h2><a href="/observer.json" class="text-button">[ RAW SNAPSHOT ]</a></div><p class="fine">Published snapshot of a local observer, not a live dashboard. Public run records, one read per hour, deterministic work only. Source sample costs are not BATTERY expenses.</p><div id="observer-summary" role="status">Loading published snapshot...</div><pre id="observer-grid" class="slot-grid" aria-label="Observed hourly slots"></pre><div id="observer-records"></div><p class="fine">[x] Recorded job / [.] no recorded job. Missing hours are not backfilled. A worker change resumes this same local ledger; it does not migrate a third-party agent.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>OFFLINE REPLAY</h2><p>72 logical tasks. One crash and worker change. Zero duplicate paper charges; $1 protected floor retained. Logical hours are not elapsed uptime.</p><a href="/proof.json" class="text-button">[ DATED EVIDENCE ]</a></section>''','<script type="module" src="/status.mjs"></script>')
quick='''unzip battery-pilot-kit.zip -d battery-kit
cd battery-kit
python3 -m unittest -v test_battery.py
python3 paper_replay.py'''
shell('docs','Developer docs',head('04 / OPERATOR MANUAL','RESERVE. DISPATCH.<br>RECONCILE.','For an agent whose runtime you control.<br>Start with a paper ledger.')+f'''<div class="docs-layout"><nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Documentation"><a href="#quickstart">[ QUICKSTART ]</a><a href="#integration">[ INTEGRATION ]</a><a href="#limits">[ LIMITS ]</a><a href="#privacy">[ DATA ]</a></nav><div><section id="quickstart" class="panel"><h2>01 / LOCAL QUICKSTART</h2><p>Download the kit. Install Python 3.10+ and Node 18+. Run these commands in a terminal from the folder containing the ZIP. No packages, keys or model payments are required.</p><a href="/battery-pilot-kit.zip" download class="text-button">[ DOWNLOAD LOCAL KIT ]</a><pre class="code">{quick}</pre><p>The tests check reservations, stale workers, duplicate receipts and reconciliation. The replay uses bundled public cost observations in a temporary SQLite ledger. It makes no network or paid model calls.</p></section><section id="integration" class="panel"><h2>02 / THE OPERATOR CONTRACT</h2><ol class="workflow"><li><strong>Configure.</strong> Set protected floor, daily cap and maximum job cost in integer microUSD (1 USD = 1,000,000).</li><li><strong>Reserve.</strong> Supply a worst-case quote and trusted provider allowance. Approve the alternate route before dispatch.</li><li><strong>Dispatch.</strong> Fence the previous worker with a new runtime epoch. A reserve is not provider credit.</li><li><strong>Settle.</strong> Reconcile the actual receipt, including incurred costs of failed jobs. Unknown outcomes keep their hold.</li><li><strong>Checkpoint.</strong> Export confirmed application results. Retain the authoritative ledger when changing local workers.</li></ol><p>Bundled <code>core.py</code> exposes <code>configure</code>, <code>credit_paper</code>, <code>takeover</code>, <code>reserve</code>, <code>dispatch</code>, <code>settle</code> and <code>checkpoint</code>. Read <code>workers.py</code> and <code>paper_replay.py</code> for runnable examples.</p></section><section id="limits" class="panel"><h2>03 / WHERE THE GUARANTEE ENDS</h2><p>Trusted local operator, one authoritative SQLite ledger. Supplied quotes, time and provider allowance are trusted inputs. The kit does not fetch billing balances or authenticate receipts.</p><p>A checkpoint hash checks integrity; it is not a signature or proof that the data is true. External paid effects require provider idempotency or a durable outbox and receipt integration.</p><p>The browser lab assumes one task/hour, a $30 daily cap, a $500 alternate allowance and a cheaper route at 40% of task cost. Fees ON adds an assumed $2/hour. These are fixed illustrative assumptions, not predictions. Reserve inputs use $5 increments, task costs $0.10, and protected balance/provider allowance whole dollars.</p></section><section id="privacy" class="panel"><h2>04 / YOUR WORKSPACE</h2><p>Policies and test history live in this browser's local storage. No account or cloud sync. Clearing site data removes them. Workspaces are separate for each domain. Export JSON from Policies before changing domains or devices, then import on the new site.</p><p>Imports are validated and merged by record ID; existing IDs are retained. Maximum 100 policies, 200 tests and 250 KB per file. Result hours are recomputed from the policy, never trusted from an imported result.</p><p>Share links include reserve, task cost, protected balance, allowance and switches in the URL fragment. They do not include your saved name or history. Anyone with the link can read the parameters; do not put secrets in policy names or files.</p><p>The public observer snapshot contains selected counts and timestamps. There is no wallet connection or paid checkout. Hosting infrastructure may process ordinary request metadata.</p><a href="/assets/brand/battery-brand-kit.zip" download class="text-button">[ ASCII LOGO + BANNER KIT ]</a></section></div></div>''')
